1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,292
Most people save what's left after rent and bills.

2
00:00:04,242 --> 00:00:06,391
That's backwards.

3
00:00:06,391 --> 00:00:09,151
The surplus never shows up.

4
00:00:09,151 --> 00:00:10,727
Flip it.

5
00:00:10,727 --> 00:00:17,836
The day your salary lands, a fixed rupee amount auto-invests — before you can spend it.

6
00:00:17,836 --> 00:00:20,115
Pay yourself first.

7
00:00:20,115 --> 00:00:24,060
That's an auto SIP: one standing instruction.

8
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:27,263
Willpower fails on a Friday night.

9
00:00:27,263 --> 00:00:30,258
A standing instruction does not.

10
00:00:30,258 --> 00:00:35,596
You never have to remember, bargain, or skip just this month.

11
00:00:35,596 --> 00:00:41,534
Because you buy on a schedule, not a mood, you average your buys over time.

12
00:00:41,534 --> 00:00:43,109
Quiet.

13
00:00:43,109 --> 00:00:44,867
Automatic.

14
00:00:44,867 --> 00:00:47,849
That's how the habit builds wealth.

15
00:00:47,849 --> 00:00:52,719
This week, set one auto SIP for a number you can live with.

16
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,932
Then leave it alone.

17
00:00:54,932 --> 00:00:58,695
Educational, not investment advice.

